require ["fileinto", "mailbox"];

# Vectis global spam-filing rule (sieve_before).
#
# rspamd's milter_headers "spam-header" routine stamps X-Spam: Yes on every
# message scoring at or above the add_header (spam) threshold. This files those
# into Junk and stops, so spam never reaches INBOX. Runs before any per-user
# sieve script, so users can still add their own rules (including allowlisting a
# sender back out of Junk) on top.
#
# Wired in via `sieve_before` in dovecot.conf only when rspamd.file_spam_to_junk
# is enabled (the default). Mounted read-only at the path below; Pigeonhole
# compiles the .svbin alongside it in the container's own writable layer.
if header :is "X-Spam" "Yes" {
    fileinto :create "Junk";
    stop;
}
